  walkthrough:
    - The plugin adds thirteen modules: the twelve listed and McpServer. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-code/dx.config.ts#config
    - NavigationTargetResolver contributes a resolver that maps a CodeProject to its graph path, not a github: key to a file. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-code/src/capabilities/navigation-target-resolver.ts
    - SpecSync loads spec sync in the browser and the desktop app once the client and settings are ready. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-code/src/capabilities/spec-sync.ts
    - BuildRunState provides the build and run results of each project when the plugin starts. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-code/src/capabilities/build-run-state.ts
  note: |
    NavigationTargetResolver maps a CodeProject object to its graph path (`NavigationResolver.forType`); it does not
    resolve a github: key to a spec or file. An `McpServer` module (the DXOS Introspect server) is added but not listed. BuildRunState holds the in-browser build and run results, not a "build
    agent"; Schema also registers SourceFile. The introspect sanity test (opt-in, `INTROSPECT_REAL=1`) finds the plugin,
    its surfaces and schemas, but no test activates the plugin's modules.
```

