    - SpecSync loads sync only in the browser and the desktop app. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-code/src/capabilities/spec-sync.ts
    - The sync capability marks sync unavailable when the file system does not answer, and runs it otherwise. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-code/src/capabilities/spec-sync.ts
    - FileSystem.get() picks the Tauri backend or the dev route. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/src/types/FileSystem.ts#get
    - fileSystemPlugin serves the `/__dx/fs` route in the dev server and refuses writes that are not `.mdl`. github:dxos/dxos/packages/apps/composer-app/src/vite/file-system.ts#fileSystemPlugin
  note: |
    `FileSystem.get()` picks the Tauri backend or the dev route. The capability marks sync unavailable when the route's
    `/roots` answers with anything but JSON, which a deployed app does. Sync writes only to keys that end in `.mdl`
    (`getSpecKey` keeps spec keys only); the Tauri backend itself does not limit suffixes. sync.test.ts uses an
    in-memory FileSystem for the root helpers; neither backend nor the sync loop is tested.
```

